✅ 1. Algorithm
Problem Statement:
Find the equilibrium index of an array. An index i is an equilibrium index if the sum of elements to the left of i is equal to the sum of elements to the right of i.

Algorithm Steps:
Calculate the total sum of the array.
Initialize left_sum = 0.
Loop through the array from index 0 to n-1:
Compute right_sum = total_sum - left_sum - arr[i]
If left_sum == right_sum, return i (equilibrium index found)
Update left_sum = left_sum + arr[i]
If no equilibrium index is found, return -1.

💻 2. Python Program
def find_equilibrium_index(arr):
    total_sum = sum(arr)
    left_sum = 0
    for i in range(len(arr)):
        right_sum = total_sum - left_sum - arr[i]
        if left_sum == right_sum:
            return i  # Found equilibrium index
        left_sum += arr[i]
  
    return -1  # No equilibrium index found

# Example usage
arr = [-7, 1, 5, 2, -4, 3, 0]
index = find_equilibrium_index(arr)

if index != -1:
    print(f"Equilibrium index is: {index}")
else:
    print("No equilibrium index found.")

